<task id="010" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>`ICommunicationEnrichmentService` — direction-agnostic enrichment for inbound AND outbound (+ missing outbound RAG)</title>
    <phase>Wave 1 — Server: enrichment + deterministic engine</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>7</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>005, 006</dependencies>
    <blocks>011, 052</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Creates new service in `Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication`; wires it into two live pipelines (inbound processor + outbound send); adds a BFF surface with DI registration; must respect ADR-010 / ADR-013 / ADR-028 / ADR-045 and the binding `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` governance checklist.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1-spine-entry</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-08</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Create `ICommunicationEnrichmentService` — a single, direction-agnostic orchestrator with the signature `EnrichAsync(Guid communicationId, CommunicationDirection direction, NormalizedMessage message, Guid? archivedDocumentId, CancellationToken ct)`. It is invoked by BOTH `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` (inbound path) AND the outbound creator(s) in `CommunicationService` (post-send), giving inbound and outbound communications identical treatment. This closes the two current outbound gaps: outbound sends are neither auto-associated nor RAG-indexed today.

    The service owns, IN ORDER: (1) association (delegates to the Association Engine — in W1 task 011 this is the refactored resolver; for task 010, delegate to the existing `IncomingAssociationResolver` seam so the entry point lands first), (2) categorization (new content-class + urgency signals), (3) AI analysis enqueue (`EnqueueDocumentAnalysisAsync`), (4) RAG indexing via `IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer` — this ADDS the missing OUTBOUND half so both directions index, (5) Responsive-Intelligence trigger (emit a `communication_assessed` assessment event; the consumer wiring lands in W5 — task 010 emits, does not consume).

    Every step is BEST-EFFORT and NON-FATAL: a failure in any step MUST NOT fail the send or the inbound-capture path (NFR-06). Preserve that invariant exactly as the current inbound processor does.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/`. Fluent in ADR-010 (DI minimalism via `CommunicationModule`), ADR-013 (AI PublicContracts facade — no direct AI-internal injection into CRUD code), ADR-028 (central `TokenCredential`/`IGraphClientFactory`; never `new` a credential), ADR-045 (the new Communication ADR authored in task 005), and the binding `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` governance checklist for BFF additions.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A new `ICommunicationEnrichmentService` + implementation exists in `Services/Communication/`, registered via `CommunicationModule`. `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` calls it on the inbound path; `CommunicationService` outbound send calls it post-send. Both directions now run association → categorization → AI analysis → RAG indexing → assessment-event emission, in that order, best-effort and non-fatal. Outbound communications auto-associate and RAG-index for the first time. Build clean; `dotnet test` green; publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported in the PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Today the inbound pipeline (`IncomingCommunicationProcessor`) performs association + analysis + indexing, but the outbound send path (`CommunicationService.SendAsync` and its record creators) does neither — outbound `sprk_communication` rows are created without association and their `.eml`/attachments are never RAG-indexed (spec §FR-08, requirement #6). R4 fixes this by hoisting the shared logic into ONE direction-agnostic service invoked from both paths (direction symmetry, per project MUST rules).

      `NormalizedMessage` is the normalized envelope the Association Engine consumes (fully defined in task 011: `{ direction, from, to[], cc[], subject, bodyText, bodyHtml, internetMessageId, inReplyTo, references[], conversationId, sentAt, attachments[] }`). Task 010 introduces the type (or a minimal version of it) and the enrichment entry point; task 011 refactors the resolver to operate over it. Order matters: 010 lands the service + wiring + envelope skeleton; 011 depends on 010.

      RAG indexing already exists for the inbound/upload path via `IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer` (`Services/Ai/IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer.cs`). Task 010 calls it for outbound too, using `archivedDocumentId` (the `.eml`/attachment document id) when present.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingAssociationResolver.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/CommunicationDirection.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PostUploadIndexingEnqueuer.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">FR-08: signature MUST be direction-agnostic `(communicationId, direction, NormalizedMessage, archivedDocumentId?)`; MUST be invoked by BOTH `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` and the `CommunicationService` outbound creators.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Order is fixed: association → categorization → AI analysis (`EnqueueDocumentAnalysisAsync`) → RAG indexing (`IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer`) → Responsive-Intelligence trigger (emit assessment event).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06">Best-effort, non-fatal: any enrichment step failing MUST NOT fail the send or inbound-capture path. Wrap each step; log and continue.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">RAG indexing MUST cover OUTBOUND (the currently-missing half) as well as inbound — both directions index.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Register via `CommunicationModule` only. No DI registration outside that module.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Use the `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/` facade for AI capability; do NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService` or other AI-internal types directly into this Communication-layer service.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Inject central `TokenCredential`/`IGraphClientFactory`/canonical Dataverse interfaces; never `new` a credential or `ConfidentialClientApplication`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">Enrichment service is codified in ADR-045; confirm this implementation aligns with the ADR authored in task 005.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">W5 consumes the emitted assessment event; task 010 EMITS only (no `EventRulesService` wiring here — that is task 052, gated by 050).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">bff-extensions Placement Justification REQUIRED in the PR (per CLAUDE.md §10), even though the answer is "stays in Services/Communication".</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Publish-size delta MUST be reported (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs, 2026-07-08; ceiling ≤60 MB). This task adds no packages; delta expected ≈ 0.</constraint>
  </constraints>

