  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs` to map the exact inbound sequence (association → analysis → indexing) and the best-effort wrapping idiom currently used.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `CommunicationService.cs` to locate the outbound send + `sprk_communication` record creator(s) — the post-send point where enrichment must be invoked.</step>
    <step order="3">Read `IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer.cs` + `PostUploadIndexingEnqueuer.cs` to confirm the enqueue signature and how `archivedDocumentId` maps to it.</step>
    <step order="4">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` (§F test obligation, §F.1 asymmetric-registration, §G hot-path) and `.claude/adr/ADR-013` PublicContracts facade rule before designing the AI-analysis hop.</step>
    <step order="5">Define `NormalizedMessage` (minimal envelope skeleton with the FR-09 fields) and `ICommunicationEnrichmentService.EnrichAsync(Guid communicationId, CommunicationDirection direction, NormalizedMessage message, Guid? archivedDocumentId, CancellationToken ct)` in `Services/Communication/`. Note in an XML doc comment that task 011 finalizes the envelope shape.</step>
    <step order="6">Implement `CommunicationEnrichmentService`: the five ordered steps, EACH wrapped best-effort/non-fatal (try/catch → log warning → continue). Step 1 delegates association to the existing `IncomingAssociationResolver` seam (task 011 swaps this for the Engine); step 3 uses `EnqueueDocumentAnalysisAsync`; step 4 uses `IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer` for BOTH directions; step 5 emits a `communication_assessed` assessment event (emit-only — no consumer here).</step>
    <step order="7">Wire the entry point into `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` (inbound) and `CommunicationService` outbound creator (post-send). Inbound may replace the inline sequence with a delegated call to preserve identical behavior; confirm no behavior change on the inbound path.</step>
    <step order="8">Register `ICommunicationEnrichmentService` → `CommunicationEnrichmentService` in `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010). Unconditional registration (endpoint/processor consume it unconditionally per ADR-032).</step>
    <step order="9">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` — confirm clean. Then `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication` — existing tests green (new enrichment/direction-symmetry tests are added in task 017).</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/r4-010-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (state the PDB convention). Expected ≈ 0.</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: invoke `code-review` on the diff; invoke `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus ADR-010/013/028/045 + NFR-06). Address Critical findings; cite the bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before opening the PR (BFF hot-path; confirm no overlap with `Services/Ai/` owners on the RAG/analysis seams — consume PublicContracts, do not fork).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (010 ✅) and `current-task.md` per task-execute protocol; advance to next pending task; record decisions (e.g., envelope-skeleton-now vs full-in-011).</step>
  </steps>

