  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`ICommunicationEnrichmentService.EnrichAsync` exists with signature `(Guid communicationId, CommunicationDirection direction, NormalizedMessage message, Guid? archivedDocumentId, CancellationToken)`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`IncomingCommunicationProcessor` invokes `EnrichAsync` on the inbound path; inbound behavior is unchanged (existing tests pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`CommunicationService` outbound send invokes `EnrichAsync` post-send.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Enrichment executes the five steps in order: association → categorization → AI analysis → RAG indexing → assessment-event emission.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Outbound path now enqueues RAG indexing via `IPostUploadIndexingEnqueuer` (the previously-missing outbound half).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each step is best-effort: a thrown exception in any step is caught, logged, and does not fail the send or inbound-capture path (NFR-06).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Service is registered in `CommunicationModule` (unconditional); no DI registration added elsewhere.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No AI-internal types injected directly (ADR-013 PublicContracts facade honored); no `new` credential (ADR-028).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; Communication unit tests pass; publish-size delta ≈ 0 reported; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Task 010 lands the entry point + wiring FIRST so task 011 (Association Engine refactor) can plug the Engine into step 1. The `NormalizedMessage` type introduced here is finalized (all FR-09 fields + provenance) in task 011.

    Per-direction + per-step tests (including direction-symmetry) are authored in task 017 — this task's acceptance criteria reference behavior verified there; task 010 implements, task 017 verifies.

    The assessment event is EMIT-ONLY here. The `EventRulesService.FireAsync("communication_assessed")` consumer wiring is task 052 (W5), gated by the 050 coordination gate with `spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2`.
  </notes>

